  "goodToKnow": "Der Parasit is a parasite: Zecken, Flöhe und Würmer sind Parasiten. Applied to people, it's an insult; the Nazis used Parasit and Schmarotzer to dehumanise Jews, so such language is avoided in German public debate today. In nature, der Schmarotzer is also used for parasitic plants and animals. It's a weak noun: den Parasiten. Parasitär means parasitic. Plural: die Parasiten."
